# Clock Time Picker — an analog Skia clock beside a snapping list of 20 times
# (1:00 pm .. 10:30 pm, 30 min apart); the scroll offset is interpolated into a
# timestamp on the UI thread and the clock's hour/minute hands follow it
# continuously (also between snap points).
# What this test covers: stepping one slot at a time (hands sweep 30 min),
# a drag held between two slots (minute hand mid-way), flings to the last
# slot and overscroll past it (interpolation extends beyond the last time),
# stepping back up, a fling stopped by a touch, and drags that start outside
# the list (ignored). Never pulls down at the list's top (that is the app's
# close gesture). List column: x ~266, rows 30pt, selected row y ~438.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/clock-time-picker"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait "text" "1:00 pm" 30000
wait 1000
# One slot at a time.
gesture pan 266 480 0 -30 700
wait 800
gesture pan 266 480 0 -30 700
wait 800
gesture pan 266 480 0 -60 900
wait 800
# Held between two slots.
gesture pan 266 480 0 -15 1500
wait 800
# A fling, then fast drags of three slots each to the end, then overscroll.
swipe 266 490 266 390
wait 600
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -90 300
wait 400
gesture pan 266 490 0 -100 500
wait 1200
wait "text" "10:30 pm" 8000
# Back up a few slots.
gesture pan 266 420 0 30 700
wait 800
gesture pan 266 420 0 60 700
wait 800
# Fling up and stop it with a touch.
swipe 266 490 266 390
wait 100
press 266 438
wait 800
# Drags outside the list (on the clock / card): no scroll.
gesture pan 135 437 0 -60 500
wait 500
gesture pan 300 600 -100 0 500
wait 1000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
